{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/564212-storytelling-the-hunt","id":564212,"title":"Storytelling the Hunt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-22T10:03:06-07:00","id":564212,"title":"Storytelling the Hunt","content":"Hi everyone.<br /> <br /> This is a bit of a big question to fit into one post but I figured i'd ask around and see what everyone thought.<br /> <br /> I've been reading the 2nd ed book on and off since it released and obviously everyone knows that Uratha are all about hunting. The hunt is life and the central concept of the game which i'm a huge fan of. The difficulty i'm having here is understanding not necessarily what the hunt IS, but how to go about storytelling this for my PC's. I've contemplated giving them multiple hunts simultaneously and letting them assign priority and I've also revealed a threat to make it hunt worthy. Both seem to have worked well but ideally i'd like to instill a bit of proactive nature to my pack and their decisions on what to hunt. <br /> <br /> To add, I've been running a WtF 2nd ed game for the last few months and my pack is starting to get their hands dirty with the day to day life of their territory along route 66. What i'm looking for is perhaps your take on how you structure a hunt and how you introduce this to your packs. Furthermore, if you have an resources that you consult on putting hunts together I'm all ears (eyes in this case).<br /> <br /> Thanks for your input in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4590-handriel","name":"Handriel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4590_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:21:13-07:00","id":564433,"title":"","content":"I'm not really sure how to address this. It seems to me that pretty much anything you do is the Hunt. Just using the mechanics of the game lends itself to hunting. You propose an antagonist situtation, and the hunt begins. During play, play up things by saying &quot;your prey,&quot; and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T00:26:31-07:00","id":565073,"title":"","content":"How players hunt is their own agency, many times over as colored by the Blood archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}